# Constitution Enforcement

The file `docs/00-vision/Afterlife-Framework-Constitution.md` is **foundational project law**.

## Agent Requirements

1. Read the Constitution before proposing architecture, gameplay, Hub, or tooling changes.
2. Reject or redesign any change that violates an Article.
3. Do not “temporarily” bypass Articles for demos, convenience, or speed.
4. Treat Constitutional amendments as rare RFC-level decisions only.
5. When uncertain, apply the Constitution’s Final Principle: favor modularity, extensibility, discoverability, maintainability, and community creativity.

## Quick Article Map

| Article | Do not |
|---------|--------|
| I | Turn the framework into a single game |
| II | Put gameplay systems in maps |
| III | Require objectives / quest arrows / forced tutorials |
| IV–V | Hardcode irreplaceable systems or content lists |
| VI | Bypass the Event Bus for cross-system coupling |
| VII | Trust clients / assume singleplayer |
| VIII–X | Ship non-extensible or anti-modding features |
| XI | Break maps without migration |
| XII–XIII | Lock to Steam Workshop or one store platform |
| XIV–XVI | Skip docs, skip RFCs, write clever unreadable code |
| XVII–XVIII | Close the source or chase clones over pillars |
